window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"t":"Strata Mundi Wiki","u":"index.html","s":"Welcome Welcome to the Strata Mundi wiki, \"the layers of the world\"! It's a block-based building and exploration game: an endless world, calculated from a seed, for you to roam, dig and reshape as you please. For now (v0.1), you play in creative mode : every block is within reach, you can fly, and you build without limits. The world [LORE TO WRITE] Finding your way around the wiki Blocks : one page per block, with its infobox (identifier, category, properties), where to find it and how to use it. Biomes : the world's landscapes, their ground and their vegetation. Commands : everything the cons"},{"t":"What's new","u":"news.html","s":"Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-29) Desert — Added Forest — Added Mountains — Added Ocean — Added Plains — Added Snowy Tundra — Added Bedrock — Added Cactus — Added Coal Ore — Added Deep Coal Ore — Added Deep Diamond Ore — Added Deep Gold Ore — Added Deep Iron Ore — Added Deep Stone — Added Diamond Ore — Added Dirt — Added Fir Needles — Added Fir Log — Added Fir Planks — Added Glass — Added Gold Ore — Added Grass Block — Added Gravel — Added Ice — Added Iron Ore — Added Oak Leaves — Added Oak Log — Added Oak Planks — Added Sand — Added Sandstone — Added Snow Block — Added Snowy Grass Block — Added Ston"},{"t":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html","s":"Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-29) Desert — Added Forest — Added Mountains — Added Ocean — Added Plains — Added Snowy Tundra — Added Bedrock — Added Cactus — Added Coal Ore — Added Deep Coal Ore — Added Deep Diamond Ore — Added Deep Gold Ore — Added Deep Iron Ore — Added Deep Stone — Added Diamond Ore — Added Dirt — Added Fir Needles — Added Fir Log — Added Fir Planks — Added Glass — Added Gold Ore — Added Grass Block — Added Gravel — Added Ice — Added Iron Ore — Added Oak Leaves — Added Oak Log — Added Oak Planks — Added Sand — Added Sandstone — Added Snow Block — Added Snowy Grass Block — Added Ston"},{"t":"Bedrock","u":"blocks/strata/bedrock.html","s":"Description Bedrock is the floor of the world. A rough, dark, stubborn layer laid at the very bottom so that nothing slips out underneath. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give bedrock . In the world, it lines the bottom of every column: one continuous row at the very bottom, topped with a few scattered blocks that make its surface bumpy. Caves never carve into it. Usage In creative, it's a decorative block with plenty of character. In survival, it will be a hard limit: whatever lies beneath stays out of reach. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. It is unbre"},{"t":"Cactus","u":"blocks/strata/cactus.html","s":"Description The cactus, prickly king of the desert. Green, ribbed, bristling with spines, it grows bolt upright and never asks to be watered. The ideal housemate. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give cactus . In the world, it only grows in the desert, on sand , as small columns a few blocks tall, scattered among the dunes. Usage Desert decoration, dry gardens, very dissuasive fences (in looks, at least). Behaviour A solid, motionless block. For now, it doesn't prick : damage arrives with survival. It doesn't grow after the world is generated either, and in creative"},{"t":"Coal Ore","u":"blocks/strata/coal_ore.html","s":"Description Grey stone speckled with matte black spots: coal. It's the most common ore in the world, the one you bump into around every cave corner. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give coal_ore . In the world, it forms small veins in stone, over a very wide range of heights: from the depths right up into the mountainsides, where it sometimes shows in the open air. In deep stone, it takes the form of deep coal ore. Usage For now, it's a decorative block that looks nice in a stone wall. Ores can't be harvested yet : breaking one in creative simply makes it vanish. I"},{"t":"Deep Coal Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_coal_ore.html","s":"Description The deep version of coal ore: black spots set into deep stone, dark on dark. You need a sharp eye to spot it, but it's definitely there. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_coal_ore . In the world, it appears instead of coal ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone, so in the depths of every biome. Usage A decorative block for now. Like every ore, it can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish without leaving anything behind. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the same family as deep stone, and harder than it"},{"t":"Deep Diamond Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_diamond_ore.html","s":"Description Sky-blue crystals set into deep stone, shining like stars in an ink-black sky. This is the form in which diamond truly shows itself in the world. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_diamond_ore . In the world, it lies at the very bottom, just above bedrock, in very small, very rare veins. With the base pack, the whole diamond zone is in deep stone: so this is the variant you'll find while exploring. Usage A decorative block for now, and the most prestigious of all. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A f"},{"t":"Deep Gold Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_gold_ore.html","s":"Description Gold in deep stone: yellow nuggets that stand out all the more against the dark background. A little treasure of the depths. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_gold_ore . In the world, it replaces gold ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone. It's the form in which you'll meet gold most often. Usage A decorative block for now. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the deep stone family, and harder than ordinary gold ore (which will matter in survival). Tips The c"},{"t":"Deep Iron Ore","u":"blocks/strata/deep_iron_ore.html","s":"Description Iron from the depths: rusty flecks on a deep stone background. Harder to spot than its stone cousin, but just as promising. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_iron_ore . In the world, it replaces iron ore wherever a vein runs through deep stone, in the depths of every biome. Usage A decorative block for now. It can't be harvested yet : in creative, breaking it makes it vanish. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block, from the deep stone family, and harder than ordinary iron ore (which will matter in survival). Tips In deep caves, iron is one o"},{"t":"Deep Stone","u":"blocks/strata/deep_stone.html","s":"Description Darker and denser than ordinary stone, deep stone tells you that you are seriously far below the surface. It looks a bit grumpy; that's only because it carries the rest of the world on its back. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give deep_stone . In the world, it replaces stone below a certain depth, in every biome. The border between the two isn't perfectly flat: it wobbles by a few blocks. Further down still, you reach bedrock. Usage Dark-toned building, cellar floors, contrast with pale stone. It's also the rock that hosts the deep variants of the ores"},{"t":"Diamond Ore","u":"blocks/strata/diamond_ore.html","s":"Description Stone studded with sparkling sky-blue crystals: diamond, the rarest and most coveted of ores. Finding it is a bit like finding a four-leaf clover underground. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give diamond_ore . In the world, diamond is only found at the very bottom, just above bedrock, in very small veins. With the base pack, that whole zone lies in deep stone: so you'll almost always meet deep diamond ore there, and rarely if ever this stone version. It remains available for building and for packs that change the world's layers. Usage A decorative block"},{"t":"Dirt","u":"blocks/strata/dirt.html","s":"Description Good old dirt: brown, crumbly, comforting. It hides under the grass and smells lovely after the rain (well, it will, once it rains). Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give dirt . In the world, it forms a layer a few blocks thick under the surface of plains, forests, mountains and snowy tundra, between the grass and the stone. It's also the bottom face of grass blocks. Usage Earthworks, artificial hills, first makeshift huts. It goes down anywhere and comes off just as fast. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. For now, dirt stays dirt: grass doesn'"},{"t":"Fir Needles","u":"blocks/strata/fir_leaves.html","s":"Description Deep green fir needles, packed into dense sprigs. They smell of winter and give the mountains their greeting-card silhouette. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give fir_leaves . In the world, they form the cone-shaped crown of firs, on mountain slopes and in the snowy tundra. Usage Hand-made festive trees, evergreen hedges, chalet roofs, artificial alpine forests. Behaviour A solid but see-through block: you can see through the gaps between the sprigs, neighbouring needles included. Like oak leaves, they don't fall when you cut the trunk, and you can walk"},{"t":"Fir Log","u":"blocks/strata/fir_log.html","s":"Description A fir trunk, darker and slimmer than an oak's, with deeply furrowed bark. It has spent its whole life in the cold and it shows: this log has character. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give fir_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of firs, which grow on mountain slopes and, more sparsely, in the snowy tundra. They take root on grass blocks, snowy or not. Usage Chalets, mountain huts, dark beams that contrast with pale planks. Laid on its side, it makes lovely railings. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like every log, it is oriented : upright when place"},{"t":"Fir Planks","u":"blocks/strata/fir_planks.html","s":"Description Dark brown fir planks with tight grain, smelling sweetly of resin and mountain chalets. Darker than oak planks, they give character to any room. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give fir_planks . They don't appear in nature; the creative inventory is their only source until crafting arrives. Usage Chalets, imaginary libraries, hulls of boats that never leave the dock, dark rafters. They go very well with stone and sandstone. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. Like oak planks, they neither burn nor rot for now. Tips A fir-plank roof on stone wal"},{"t":"Glass","u":"blocks/strata/glass.html","s":"Description A clear pane with a thin frame, through which you can admire the landscape without catching a cold. Glass is the promise of a bright, airy home. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give glass . It never appears in nature: it's a builder's product through and through. Usage Windows, glass roofs, greenhouses, aquariums, underwater observatories. Anything that needs to see outside (or inside). Behaviour A solid, transparent block: only its frame is drawn, the rest lets everything show through. You can walk on it without trouble. Two glass blocks side by side "},{"t":"Gold Ore","u":"blocks/strata/gold_ore.html","s":"Description Stone gleaming with little bright-yellow nuggets: gold, gold! The kind of block that makes you squeal with joy around a cave bend. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give gold_ore . In the world, gold hides in the lower half of the world, in veins smaller and rarer than iron's. Since its heights mostly dip into deep stone, you'll meet it far more often in its deep form; in stone, it only shows up in a thin band just above the deep layer. Usage A decorative block for now, and what a decoration! Ores can't be harvested yet : breaking it in creative makes it "},{"t":"Grass Block","u":"blocks/strata/grass_block.html","s":"Description The grass block is the world's green carpet: neatly mown grass on top, a green fringe spilling over the sides, and dirt underneath. It makes you want to have a picnic. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give grass_block . In the world, it covers the ground of plains, forests and mountains, until the stone and snow of the peaks take over. By the water's edge, it gives way to shoreline sand or gravel. Usage Gardens, lawns, green roofs. It's also where oaks and firs take root when the world is generated. Behaviour A full, opaque block, with different textures"},{"t":"Gravel","u":"blocks/strata/gravel.html","s":"Description A cheerful jumble of little pebbles, grey, beige and brown. Gravel never quite managed to become stone, but it kept its good mood. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give gravel . In the world, it carpets the ocean floor and forms the shores and shallow beds along forests, mountains and snowy tundra. Usage Garden paths, mountain trails, the banks of an artificial river. It gives a natural, slightly rustic look to anything it touches. Behaviour A full, opaque block. Like sand, it doesn't fall yet : until gravity arrives, it stays perched wherever you put it"},{"t":"Ice","u":"blocks/strata/ice.html","s":"Description Water that got a little too chilly. Ice is translucent and bluish, hinting at what lies beneath, like a display case laid over the lake. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give ice . In the world, it covers the surface of the snowy tundra's waters: a single layer, at sea level, with liquid water right underneath. Usage Skating rinks (no sliding yet), frosted windows, snow palaces. It also forms a natural bridge to walk across frozen lakes. Behaviour A solid, translucent block: you can see through it, slightly tinted. It's safe to walk on. For now it neithe"},{"t":"Iron Ore","u":"blocks/strata/iron_ore.html","s":"Description Stone sprinkled with small rust-coloured and beige flecks: iron. Low-key but widespread, it's the serious member of the gang, the one that will go far. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give iron_ore . In the world, it forms small veins in stone, over a wide range of heights, from the depths to well up under the hills. A little less common than coal. In deep stone, it becomes deep iron ore. Usage A decorative block for now: ores can't be harvested yet , and breaking one in creative simply makes it vanish. It will come into its own with survival. Behaviour"},{"t":"Oak Leaves","u":"blocks/strata/oak_leaves.html","s":"Description Bushy, bright green oak foliage, full of little gaps through which you can glimpse the sky. Perfect for a nap in the shade (symbolic shade, until light arrives). Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give oak_leaves . In the world, they form the rounded crown of oaks, in plains and forests. Usage Hedges, bushes, green roofs, garden mazes, camouflaged tree houses. Behaviour A solid but see-through block: you can see through the gaps in the foliage, neighbouring leaves included. For now, leaves don't fall when you cut the trunk: a tree without its log proudly k"},{"t":"Oak Log","u":"blocks/strata/oak_log.html","s":"Description A handsome oak trunk with rough brown bark and clearly visible rings at each end. It smells of forests and childhood tree houses. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give oak_log . In the world, it forms the trunks of oaks, scattered in the plains and packed tightly in forests. Oaks only grow on grass blocks. Usage Beams, pillars, timber frames, window frames, rustic cabins. Laid on its side, it makes great lintels and garden benches. Behaviour A full, opaque block. The log is oriented : placed on the top or bottom of a block, it stands upright; placed agai"},{"t":"Oak Planks","u":"blocks/strata/oak_planks.html","s":"Description Oak planks in a warm golden brown, nicely planed, with even grain. The building wood par excellence: you already want to lay a rug on them. Obtaining In creative: the Building tab of the inventory, or /give oak_planks . They don't appear in nature. Until crafting arrives, the creative inventory is their only source. Usage Floors, walls, roofs, imaginary furniture, cosy houses. Paired with oak logs, they give an instant cottage look. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. It neither burns nor rots for now: your wooden houses are safe from everything except your own renovations."},{"t":"Sand","u":"blocks/strata/sand.html","s":"Description Golden sand, fine and warm, the kind that makes you want to kick off your shoes. You find it where it's hot and where there's water, which is convenient for a holiday. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give sand . In the world, it covers the whole desert (with sandstone underneath) and the land rising out of the ocean. It also forms the beaches and the shallow bed along plains and desert shores. Usage Beaches, zen gardens, giant sandcastles. It's also the only ground cacti grow on. Behaviour A full, opaque block. For now, sand doesn't fall : gravity hasn'"},{"t":"Sandstone","u":"blocks/strata/sandstone.html","s":"Description Sandstone is sand that took its time to settle down. Its sides show pretty horizontal layers, and its top is as smooth as a temple floor tile. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give sandstone . In the world, it forms a layer a few blocks thick right under the desert sand, before the stone. Usage Desert architecture, pyramids, colonnades, bathhouses. It goes beautifully with sand and fir planks. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. The top and bottom faces differ from the sides, giving striped walls and plain floors. Unlike sand, it will never need "},{"t":"Snow Block","u":"blocks/strata/snow_block.html","s":"Description A block of tightly packed snow, dazzling white with bluish glints. It crunches just from looking at it. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give snow_block . In the world, it caps the highest mountain peaks, above the band of bare stone. Careful: the snowy tundra is covered with snowy grass blocks, not snow blocks. Usage Monumental snowmen, igloos, high-altitude chalets, or simply artificial peaks for mountains of your own. Behaviour A full, opaque, motionless block. For now it never melts, not even placed in the middle of the desert: this is snow of rare d"},{"t":"Snowy Grass Block","u":"blocks/strata/snowy_grass_block.html","s":"Description A grass block wearing its woolly hat: a layer of snow on top, grass peeking shyly out of the sides, and dirt underneath. It's cold out there, but it looks perfectly cosy. Obtaining In creative: the Natural tab of the inventory, or /give snowy_grass_block . In the world, it forms the ground of the snowy tundra. Near the frozen water, the shores are made of gravel. Usage Winter landscapes, mountain villages, very early holiday decorations. The tundra's firs take root on it. Behaviour A full, opaque block, with snow on top, mixed snow-and-grass sides and dirt underneath. For now, the "},{"t":"Stone","u":"blocks/strata/stone.html","s":"Description Stone is the backbone of the world: grey, sturdy, dependable. Dig through a few blocks of dirt, sand or snow and there it is, going on for a long, long way down. Obtaining In creative, it waits for you in the Natural tab of the inventory, or through /give stone . In the world, it forms the core of every biome, under the surface layer. On the highest mountains it even pokes out into the open air, before snow takes over. Further down, it gives way to deep stone. Usage The all-purpose building block: walls, foundations, towers that tickle the clouds. It also hosts the ore veins. Behav"},{"t":"Water","u":"blocks/strata/water.html","s":"Description The water of seas, lakes and oceans, blue and translucent. It makes you want to dive in, will one day be home to fish, and always looks great on a postcard. Obtaining Water has no item : you won't find it in the creative inventory, nor with /give . In the world, it fills every dip in the terrain up to sea level, from the vast ocean to the small lakes of the plains. In the snowy tundra, its surface is frozen. Usage Scenery, natural border, landmark near the starting point. Behaviour Water is static : it neither flows nor spreads. It isn't solid, so you pass through it like air (no s"},{"t":"Blocks","u":"blocks/index.html","s":"Building Fir Planks Glass Oak Planks Natural Bedrock Cactus Coal Ore Deep Coal Ore Deep Diamond Ore Deep Gold Ore Deep Iron Ore Deep Stone Diamond Ore Dirt Fir Needles Fir Log Gold Ore Grass Block Gravel Ice Iron Ore Oak Leaves Oak Log Sand Sandstone Snow Block Snowy Grass Block Stone Other Water"},{"t":"Desert","u":"biomes/strata/desert.html","s":"Description A sea of golden sand under a vast sky, where only cacti dare to grow. The desert is hot, dry and surprisingly peaceful. Don't forget your hat. Obtaining The desert appears in hot, dry regions, on rather gentle terrain. Usage Sandstone galore right under the surface, wide open spaces for monumental builds, and cacti for decoration. Behaviour Ground : sand on the surface, then a layer of sandstone, then stone. Vegetation : cacti, which only grow on sand. Shores : sand, on the beaches as well as underwater. No trees, no grass: the contrast with neighbouring biomes shows from very far "},{"t":"Forest","u":"biomes/strata/forest.html","s":"Description A dense, lush oak forest, where the crowns almost touch and you weave your way between trunks. It smells of moss, bark and adventure. Obtaining Forests appear in temperate, humid regions, on gentle terrain. Along with the plains, it's one of the two biomes where the world can make you start . Usage An endless supply of oak logs and leaves, and the perfect setting for a tree house or an elven village… of your own invention. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks, with dirt underneath, then stone. Vegetation : lots of oaks, packed close together. Shores : gravel on the banks and on the shal"},{"t":"Mountains","u":"biomes/strata/mountains.html","s":"Description Dizzying ridges, deep valleys and snowy peaks scratching the sky. The mountains are the biome of breathtaking views and big, slightly mad projects. Obtaining Mountains rise inland, where the terrain is young and barely eroded. They form sharp ridges separated by wide valleys, and they're by far the highest terrain in the world. Usage Lookouts, clifftop castles, tunnels through the rock, and stone cliffs where ores sometimes show. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks on the slopes, with dirt underneath. Altitude : above a certain height, grass gives way to bare stone, then, higher still,"},{"t":"Ocean","u":"biomes/strata/ocean.html","s":"Description Water, water, and more water. The ocean stretches away from the continents, deep and blue, with here and there a sandy island poking its nose out. Obtaining The ocean fills the regions farthest from inland, where the ground dives well below sea level. Usage Long crossings, underwater bases, lighthouses on sandy islets, and a huge supply of gravel on the bottom. Behaviour Water : static, up to sea level. It doesn't flow and you pass through it like air. Floor : a layer of gravel, then stone. Land above water : sand, on top and underneath. Vegetation : none, for now. Caves never open"},{"t":"Plains","u":"biomes/strata/plains.html","s":"Description Wide stretches of soft grass rolling as far as the eye can see, dotted with lone oaks. The plains are the biome of picnics, long strolls and first houses. Obtaining Plains appear in temperate, rather dry regions, on gentle terrain. They're one of the two biomes where the world can make you start (along with the forest). Usage Ideal building land: flat, open, with just enough trees for decoration. Behaviour Ground : grass blocks, with a layer of dirt underneath, then stone. Vegetation : a few scattered oaks. Shores : sand, on the beaches as well as on the shallow bed. Borders with n"},{"t":"Snowy Tundra","u":"biomes/strata/snowy_tundra.html","s":"Description A vast frozen plain carpeted in snow, where a few shivering firs stand and lakes freeze into mirrors of ice. Cold, silent and pretty as a postcard. Obtaining The snowy tundra appears in the coldest regions, on gentle terrain. Usage Chalets, igloos, winter villages, and large frozen lakes you can walk across. Behaviour Ground : snowy grass blocks, with dirt underneath, then stone. Water : its surface is frozen into a layer of ice, with liquid water right underneath. Vegetation : a few scattered firs. Shores : gravel along the water. For now, snow doesn't melt and it doesn't snow: th"},{"t":"Biomes","u":"biomes/index.html","s":"Desert Forest Mountains Ocean Plains Snowy Tundra"},{"t":"/help","u":"commands/help.html","s":"/help [command] Lists the commands, or details one. Run on your screen. Description /help is the console's cheat sheet: it lists every available command, with its syntax and a one-line explanation. Lost? Always start here. Syntax /help : shows every command. /help <command> : shows only the one you asked for (without the slash). Examples /help for the complete list. /help time to remember the time keywords. Behaviour The command is handled directly by your screen, without going through the server, and answers in the language chosen in the options. It works in every game mode. An unknown comman"},{"t":"/tp","u":"commands/tp.html","s":"/tp <x> <y> <z> (~ = your position) Teleports (~5 = 5 blocks further). Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /tp teleports you instantly to precise coordinates. Ideal for exploring, finding a build again, or taking a close look at a mountain peak spotted in the distance. Syntax /tp <x> <y> <z> . Each coordinate can be: a number (decimals allowed); ~ : your own current coordinate; ~ followed by a number: an offset from your position ( ~5 , ~-10 ). Examples /tp 0 200 0 : off to the centre of the world, well above the ground. /tp ~ ~20 ~ : rise twenty blocks on the spot. /tp ~100 "},{"t":"/give","u":"commands/give.html","s":"/give <item> Puts an item in the selected slot. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /give drops an item straight into the selected slot of your hotbar. Quicker than rummaging through the creative inventory when you already know the identifier of what you want. Syntax /give <item> , where the item is an identifier: full, with its namespace: strata:stone ; or short, for the base content: stone is the same as strata:stone . Examples /give glass for a brand-new pane. /give strata:fir_log for a fir log. Behaviour Run by the server, in creative mode only. The item replaces whatever"},{"t":"/gamemode","u":"commands/gamemode.html","s":"/gamemode <creative|survival> Changes the game mode. Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /gamemode changes the game mode of the current world. In v0.1, only one mode exists, creative ; so the command is mostly here to get ready for the future. Syntax /gamemode <creative|survival> Examples /gamemode creative : switch (or switch back) to creative mode. /gamemode survival : the console kindly tells you that survival arrives in v0.3. Behaviour Run by the server. The chosen mode is saved with the world and appears in the world list. For now, asking for survival changes nothing: th"},{"t":"/time","u":"commands/time.html","s":"/time <set|add|query> [value] Sets the time (day, noon, night, midnight or ticks). Run by the server, in creative mode only. Description /time reads or sets the world clock. Each world keeps its own time, which moves forward on its own during play and is saved with the world. Syntax /time <set|add|query> [value] query : shows the current time. set <value> : sets the time, with a keyword ( day for sunrise, noon for midday, night for sunset, midnight ) or a number of ticks. add <ticks> : moves the clock forward by that many ticks. Examples /time set noon : high noon. /time query : what time is i"},{"t":"/seed","u":"commands/seed.html","s":"/seed Shows the world seed. Run by the server. Description /seed shows the world seed: the little secret code from which the whole terrain was calculated. Same seed, same world, every time. Syntax /seed , with no argument. Examples /seed : the console answers with the seed, for instance the word you typed when creating the world. Behaviour Run by the server. It's the only command available in every game mode : knowing your seed isn't cheating. If you typed some text as the seed when creating the world, that text is shown; otherwise, it's the randomly chosen number. Tips Share your seed with yo"},{"t":"/cinematic","u":"commands/cinematic.html","s":"/cinematic <id> Plays a cinematic from the packs. Run on your screen. Description /cinematic plays a cinematic: a scripted camera shot, described in a pack, that sweeps over the surroundings like in a film. The base pack contains a demonstration one. Syntax /cinematic <id> , where id is the cinematic's full identifier (namespace included). Examples /cinematic strata:showcase : the camera rises and circles around where you are. Behaviour Handled directly by your screen, in every game mode. The shot starts from your position : the same cinematic works anywhere. While it plays, you can't move, th"},{"t":"Commands","u":"commands/index.html","s":"Open the console with T or /; Tab completes, up/down recalls commands. /help Lists the commands, or details one. /tp Teleports (~5 = 5 blocks further). /give Puts an item in the selected slot. /gamemode Changes the game mode. /time Sets the time (day, noon, night, midnight or ticks). /seed Shows the world seed. /cinematic Plays a cinematic from the packs."},{"t":"World generation","u":"mechanics/world-generation.html","s":"Principle The world isn't drawn by hand: it's calculated from a seed, bit by bit as you move forward. Same seed, same world, down to the block, whatever order you explore in. It's practically endless: only the border chosen at creation stops it. Terrain and biomes Four invisible maps cover the world: temperature , humidity , continentalness (from open sea to deep inland) and erosion (from flat, worn land to young terrain). The last two give the ground height: deep oceans, gentle hills, ridged mountains. The biome, picked from the climate, only decides the ground cover and vegetation: transitio"},{"t":"Saving","u":"mechanics/saving.html","s":"Principle Each world has its own folder: its description (name, seed, mode, play time), your character (position, view direction, hotbar) and a screenshot for the world list. Since the terrain can be recalculated from the seed, only changed areas are saved: a well-explored but barely altered world stays tiny. When the game saves Automatically , at regular intervals (adjustable in Options → Game). With Save and quit , in the pause menu. When you close the game window. On the DS, when you close the lid : instant pause and save. Never a damaged world Each file is written alongside, then swapped i"},{"t":"Game modes","u":"mechanics/game-modes.html","s":"Principle The game mode decides a world's rules. It's chosen at creation, on the \"New world\" screen, and then shown in the world list. In v0.1, only one mode exists: creative . Survival arrives in v0.3. Creative mode The no-strings-attached sandbox, to build and explore in complete freedom: every block is available in the creative inventory, with tabs and search; you break blocks instantly , even bedrock; you fly by double-tapping jump; every console command is allowed; all knowledge is known in advance: there's nothing to discover before you can build. Survival (coming soon) Planned for v0.3."},{"t":"Mechanics","u":"mechanics/index.html","s":"World generation Saving Game modes"},{"t":"Controls","u":"controls.html","s":"Keyboard, mouse and gamepad Strata Mundi plays just as well with keyboard and mouse as with a gamepad , and you can switch at any time. On-screen prompts follow the last device you used: keyboard key or gamepad button. Any keyboard layout The game reads the position of keys, not the printed letter: on a French AZERTY keyboard, movement naturally lands on Z, Q, S, D. Yet the texts show the letter actually printed on your key. The gamepad Buttons are named as on a New 3DS (A on the right, B at the bottom, X at the top, Y on the left), as on the DS handheld console. Left stick to move, right stic"},{"t":"Settings","u":"settings.html","s":"Settings for every machine Strata Mundi's golden rule: everything can be turned on, off or adjusted . Whether you play on a powerful PC, an old laptop or the DS handheld console, you can tailor the game to your machine, your eyes and your habits. Each option comes with a short sentence explaining what it does, performance included. Presets A preset sets all the graphics at once: Very low , Low , Medium , High , Ultra , and DS , designed for the small home-made handheld console. Touching a single graphics setting afterwards switches to Custom , without losing anything else. Applied right away C"}];
